    "created_at": "2025-04-28T07:33:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-04-28T07:33:05Z",
    "body": "The fact that it is not standardized. It is merely a personal convention. Tools that process HTML cannot link `abbr` elements with the corresponding `dfn` elements, unless they implement heuristics that look for specific custom elements or `data-*` attributes. And even then these tools would not be generic: other HTML authors might employ a `data-for` attribute with a different meaning and different contents.\n\nI believe the link between an abbreviation and its definition is sufficiently strong and semantically meaningful that it deserves standardization.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
